{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting","id":1443041,"title":"Alcina Dimitrescu - What she would be if she was a kindred in the VTM setting.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-07T15:54:18-07:00","id":1443041,"title":"Alcina Dimitrescu - What she would be if she was a kindred in the VTM setting.","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> So I've recently read and seen some material on Resident Evil, where one the characters from there would interesting to discuss what it would be in the game vampire.<br /> The character in question is Alcina Dimitrescu, according to various material, including official - suggest a kindred of some kind, or the very least a mortal who practices vampirism. With that said, it makes good sense to consider Alcina as a kindred, as she does have powers which seems to fit well with being a kindred and other associations that fit that notion. Which raises some obvious questions if she is a vampire, like what clan she belongs to, what generation is she, what disciplines does she know and so, which obviously is going to be based on what is known. This is both challenging and interesting at the same time, but more so is an opportunity to to create a character that could be used for anyone who're interested in running something in the resident evil setting or as inspiration for a similar character. As an note important note, I'm thinking in terms of pre-V5.<br /> <br /> <br /> Currently what we know - Source: <a href=\"https://residentevil.fandom.com/wiki/Alcina_Dimitrescu\" target=\"_blank\">https://residentevil.fandom.com/wiki/Alcina_Dimitrescu</a> - Obviously some is not public knowledge in the game world:<br /> ~ there are more sources, including the game demo and other various sources, and earlier Resident Evil games, though I've only included information from RE: Village.<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Full Name: Alcina Dimitrescu<br /> ~ Lady D. or Mistress D.<br /> Gender: Female<br /> Birthdate: Unknown, before 1950.<br /> Eye Color: Yellow<br /> Skin Color: Very pale - deathlike skin color.<br /> Height: 2,9 cm. / Aprox 9 ft 6 in - <u><b>This extreme height could be from extended use of Vicissitude?</b></u><br /> Occupation: Countess of Castle Dimitrescu (At least since 1950s but possibly before.)<br /> ~ Location of the castle: Carpathian Mountains: <a href=\"https://residentevil.fandom.com/wiki/Castle_Dimitrescu\" target=\"_blank\">https://residentevil.fandom.com/wiki/Castle_Dimitrescu</a> - Which is in central Romania.<br /> Signature outfit: A long flowing white dress and a wide-brimmed dark hat, along with a black flower on her chest.<br /> Reflection: She has one. ~<b><u>That rules out Lasombra</u></b> - <b><i>Unless</i></b>.. It's possible for a Lasombra to actually have one?<br /> <br /> Her last name uses a romanian patronym and is confirmed to be romanian, and the castle is also located in Romania, which means that the clan she most likely would belong to would be clans that are usually to be found there. Also to note, the castle is specifically in the Carpathian mountains, so we can get fairly specific in what clans we're most likely dealing with.<br /> <br /> She has the ability to elongate her fingernails into razor-sharp claws, there is footage of both being turned at the same time. - This would fit well with Protean or Vicissitude.<br /> Alcina was a follower of a Satanic witch-cult which practiced vampirism and human sacrifice, possibly for sustenance. - Supports the part of being kindred, but we already assume she is.<br /> She was already regularly engaging in vampirism in the 1950s, and had successfully mutated three women by 1958. - These three &quot;mutated&quot; woman, whom she also considers her daughters, could be her kindred childer&quot; because they aren't her biological daughters?<br /> <br /> We know she is used to cruelty:<br /> &quot;This control allowed Dimitrescu's family to rule their castle with barbarous cruelty, regularly taking in new staff to replace those who were taken to the dungeon to be killed<br /> The blood of their victims was used to create an enriched red wine called <i>Sanguis Virginis</i> (Latin for &quot;Maiden's Blood&quot;).&quot; It is also known, that the family has imprisoned and tortured many of their staff/slaves, for many years, quite possible as part of creating <i>Sanguis Virginis. <u><b>~</b></u></i><u><b>The Torturing suggest Tzimisce.</b></u><br /> Since the 1950s to 2020s, the castle has been the epicenter of a number of violent murders and mutilations instigated by the nobles against the local peasantry.<br /> In the late 20th century, the castle became associated with <i>Sanguis Virginis</i>, a brand of enriched red wine marketed by Alcina - Obviously the mutilations and murders are connected with this, thus we know that she's actually still doing this. <b><u>~ All of this suggests They're part of the Sabbat.</u></b><br /> <br /> About her Childe:<br /> One has shown it has the ability to turn into partial swarm of insects that also has the buzzing insect swarm sound, although it does look more like dark dissolved matter moving through the air - which I think would suggest protean, obtenebration or a combination, but not really sure. Some of their concept art depicts these &quot;daughters&quot; as having a shadowy haze around them - hence also why I'm thinking obtenebration.Though it might also be a form of blood sorcery or ritual effect.<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Personally, I think her being of Clan Tzimisce makes very good sense, especially also due to the fact of the castle location which also is supported by what supports it's the Sabbat.<br /> About her age, how old is she really? Well, the design inspiration is from 1560. From what we can see in the official artwork, she appears at the very least to be an adult - she appears to be young, I think mid 20's to mid 30's at maximum.Today that would make her around 90-105 years old, at least. I'm not really sure if there are any indications as to what generation she might be at. Style of clothing and the fact that she is going with the same look (makeup, dress, hat, etc.) seems she's very set in her ways, to me that indicates she's very old. I'm thinking that she's definitely from the victorian age, but thats mostly based on her clothing style (hat included), but could be even earlier than this.<br /> <br /> I'm curious what you guys think, what impression do you get?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T16:20:23-07:00","id":1443046,"title":"","content":"i bloody love this! you really did capture her in a vtm way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T12:54:27-07:00","id":1443788,"title":"","content":"The strong focus on family (she references her brother and daughters) as well as the shambling zombies we've seen in the trailers give me strong Giovanni vibes. She managed to pick up Protean somehow, perhaps from whatever those monstrous werewolf-like creatures are. Until she has a monstrous transformation (which she almost certainly will, this is Resident Evil) I don't think there's a lot of support for Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T09:57:32-07:00","id":1444345,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce infernalist, or Balli maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T12:01:41-07:00","id":1444530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1443788#post1443788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The strong focus on family (she references her brother and daughters) as well as the shambling zombies we've seen in the trailers give me strong Giovanni vibes. She managed to pick up Protean somehow, perhaps from whatever those monstrous werewolf-like creatures are. Until she has a monstrous transformation (which she almost certainly will, this is Resident Evil) I don't think there's a lot of support for Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Her sheer size needs some kind of explanation when interpreted/expressed by the VtM system, the only thing I can see that makes sense, is Vicissitude, plus the fact that the origins of her family's castle, would make much more likely that she would be of the Tzimisce, Besides, necromancy is more likely to have been learned as an out of clan discipline, and all it would require for zombies to be created would be a level 3 on path of the bone (Necromancy - From DAV20) - However, we could also consider the &quot;zombies&quot; as mortals/ghouls who've been disfigured by vicissitude. But if we regard them as actual zombies, then how she's come about learning necromancy, is of course a question that needs some explaining, but the is probably much more easily explainable, than how a Giovanni kindred were able to seize a castle in the Carpathian mountains - home of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> As for her nature and demeanor, I'd say there are definitely several viable combinations, I'm curious as to which combination you feel fit her personality the most.<br /> One combination I think would make a lot of sense, would be: Nature: Autocrat. Demeanor: Bravo or Sadist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1444345#post1444345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce infernalist, or Balli maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Baali is a thought that has crossed my mind, but there are just things that needs to be explained, which I think is hard to do if it was a Baali.<br /> However, a Tzimisce infernalist is something that definitely is much more likely than being one from Baali, her being able to sprout claws (elongate her nails) would be a demonic investment.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:08:07-07:00","id":1444631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incarnate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1444530#post1444530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Her sheer size needs some kind of explanation when interpreted/expressed by the VtM system, the only thing I can see that makes sense, is Vicissitude, plus the fact that the origins of her family's castle, would make much more likely that she would be of the Tzimisce, Besides, necromancy is more likely to have been learned as an out of clan discipline, and all it would require for zombies to be created would be a level 3 on path of the bone (Necromancy - From DAV20) - However, we could also consider the &quot;zombies&quot; as mortals/ghouls who've been disfigured by vicissitude. But if we regard them as actual zombies, then how she's come about learning necromancy, is of course a question that needs some explaining, but the is probably much more easily explainable, than how a Giovanni kindred were able to seize a castle in the Carpathian mountains - home of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> As for her nature and demeanor, I'd say there are definitely several viable combinations, I'm curious as to which combination you feel fit her personality the most.<br /> One combination I think would make a lot of sense, would be: Nature: Autocrat. Demeanor: Bravo or Sadist.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Baali is a thought that has crossed my mind, but there are just things that needs to be explained, which I think is hard to do if it was a Baali.<br /> However, a Tzimisce infernalist is something that definitely is much more likely than being one from Baali, her being able to sprout claws (elongate her nails) would be a demonic investment.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Infernalism also covers her size, mystic knowledge and claws (or potentially she has enough Obfuscate to mask horrid form as normal looking but huge.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T12:35:42-07:00","id":1444698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1444631#post1444631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Infernalism also covers her size, mystic knowledge and claws (or potentially she has enough Obfuscate to mask horrid form as normal looking but huge.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate could make her size look normal<br /> I was thinking that she would have Obfuscate at level 3, at the very least, irregardless of what her size was the result of, whether it would've been from extended Vicissitude use or from infernalism, wouldn't really matter much. Though, I think the infernalist part would suit well, especially also due to the fact that her &quot;daughters&quot; are showing power use that is difficult to explain with a single discipline - being able to change into a partially formed or fully formed swarm of insects, that would most likely fit with infernalism, though I'm not sure which demonic investment this and Alcina's size increase would be.<br /> <br /> You have an idea as to what her nature and demeanor would be?<br /> Perhaps also an idea with regards to Path of Enlightenment (or road)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T21:22:27-07:00","id":1444989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incarnate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1444698#post1444698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obfuscate could make her size look normal<br /> I was thinking that she would have Obfuscate at level 3, at the very least, irregardless of what her size was the result of, whether it would've been from extended Vicissitude use or from infernalism, wouldn't really matter much. Though, I think the infernalist part would suit well, especially also due to the fact that her &amp;quot;daughters&amp;quot; are showing power use that is difficult to explain with a single discipline - being able to change into a partially formed or fully formed swarm of insects, that would most likely fit with infernalism, though I'm not sure which demonic investment this and Alcina's size increase would be.<br /> <br /> You have an idea as to what her nature and demeanor would be?<br /> Perhaps also an idea with regards to Path of Enlightenment (or road)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of Screams, maybe Path of Cruelty, or Evil Revelations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:49:18-07:00","id":1445546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1444989#post1444989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Path of Screams, maybe Path of Cruelty, or Evil Revelations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to being an Infernalist? I would assume one could still be on a different path/road, like for instance Road/Path of the Devil? Considering her Tzimisce origins, where Road of Kings or Metamorphosis is the most prevalent, especially considering her family's method of rule, I would actually think Path of the Tyrant or Perhaps the Devil.<br /> <br /> With regards to the demonic investments, which in particular would be the one that would be responsible for the size increase? I don't see any that is described to do that, perhaps I just missed it. Though with that said, I can see why it couldn't be approved or just created by an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:04:30-07:00","id":1445740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incarnate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1445546#post1445546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Due to being an Infernalist? I would assume one could still be on a different path/road, like for instance Road/Path of the Devil? Considering her Tzimisce origins, where Road of Kings or Metamorphosis is the most prevalent, especially considering her family's method of rule, I would actually think Path of the Tyrant or Perhaps the Devil.<br /> <br /> With regards to the demonic investments, which in particular would be the one that would be responsible for the size increase? I don't see any that is described to do that, perhaps I just missed it. Though with that said, I can see why it couldn't be approved or just created by an ST.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Screams and Cruelty are both Paths on the Road of the Devil, as to the size? She absorbs victims with Viscittitude, and her investments keep her beautiful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:33:27-07:00","id":1445766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1445740#post1445740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as to the size? She absorbs victims with Viscittitude, and her investments keep her beautiful...</div> </div> </div> </div>Would she be using any specific merits or combo disciplines to be able to absorb the victims, or just clever use of the the Vicissitude discpline?<br /> As to the investments that would keep her beautiful, I'm assuming that would be <i>Uncanny Beauty.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T23:53:28-07:00","id":1445785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incarnate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1445766#post1445766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would she be using any specific merits or combo disciplines to be able to absorb the victims, or just clever use of the the Vicissitude discpline?<br /> As to the investments that would keep her beautiful, I'm assuming that would be <i>Uncanny Beauty.</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The absorbing victims would have to be an amalgam or high level power she created or was given/taught, uncanny beauty works as a hand wave, basically it will not be perfect as she wasn't designed to be a VtM character, but with those abilities and gifts and a little bit os ST fiat, you can get close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:13:57-07:00","id":1445868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443041-alcina-dimitrescu-what-she-would-be-if-she-was-a-kindred-in-the-vtm-setting?p=1445785#post1445785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The absorbing victims would have to be an amalgam or high level power she created or was given/taught, uncanny beauty works as a hand wave, basically it will not be perfect as she wasn't designed to be a VtM character, but with those abilities and gifts and a little bit os ST fiat, you can get close.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to which disciplines you think it would be an amalgam of, or at what level if it is a Vicissitude only power?<br /> To answer that, I think we need to be able to answer some questions, like what exactly is happening to the victims when she is absorbing them, like is is turning them into a different material while it kills them, or are they just molded into something else - like them being transmogrified into a clay like substance? When she is absorbing, is she doing it with finesse rather than brute force, or the opposite? To me she she seems like one that would use brute force, but most certainly is capable of finesse. It's questions such as these that would help define what kind of disciplines that are being used, and there is another important question, does this power also work on kindred as well? Considering that Vicissitude is able to affect both kindred and mortals alike, it's very likely that it could.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm leaning mostly towards it being mostly a combination of advanced versions of the lower level powers of Vicissitude, but supported by a few others. The ones to me that would make the most sense, would be an advanced form of Mallable Visage, Transmogrify the Mortal Clay and Rend the Osseous Frame, because the basic versions already allows the user to make the changes those allow for, to it's own body. It begs the question, what level of Vicissitude would be required to represent that level of mastery?<br /> <br /> If she's going by the route of brute force, I definitely think several levels of Potence would be necessary. If look at Flaying Touch, which is Vicissitude and Potence amalgam, it should be pretty clear why Potence would be needed, she'd essentially be stripping material from the victims body.<br /> <br /> If we look at the amalgam power Wound Sculpting, then we see it's composed of Fortitude and Vicissitude, so I would assume when she is absorbing the victims, she'd definitely need several levels of Fortitude as well, as &quot;absorbing&quot; these victims would definitely be cause damage to her own body in the process.<br /> <br /> The last part, which is actually the fusing or bonding with the new material with her own, actually requires discipline use or not, if not, it would just be Body Crafting she'd be using, otherwise if it's a discipline, then it's probably a higher level Vicissitude, and if not, then I'm not actually sure which it would be.<br /> <br /> With regards to her uncanny beauty, I don't even think that the demonic investment necessarily is a must, as Mallable Visage allows her to restore her beauty, that is if she can recreate her own look over and over again from memory, an image or painting of her. Besides, that point, if she's only using the parts that she needs to increase her size, I don't think she would ever need to make changes to her face, only certain parts of her body.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","user":"Incarnate","date":". 04-25-2021, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}